Hermes Agent (NousResearch/hermes-agent)
----------------------------------------

Source:  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
Commit:  848fc0ad8be766b9dc10fe42bd80b5fc2d45d95c
Used in: server/engine/tools.py — wrap_untrusted(), adapted from
         agent/tool_dispatch_helpers.py (_maybe_wrap_untrusted, _neutralize_delimiters)
         server/evals/fakemodel.py — the fake model server, adapted from
         tests/fakes/fake_llm_provider.py and tests/fakes/providers/anthropic_messages.py
         server/engine/session.py — SUMMARY_PREFIX, the framing of a compaction summary,
         adapted from agent/context_compressor.py (SUMMARY_PREFIX)
         server/engine/compact.py — summarizer rules (the conversation is data, credentials
         become [REDACTED], language, dated past tense, the open request), the summary
         budget and the ineffective-compaction hold, adapted from agent/context_compressor.py
         (_build_summary_prompt, _SECTION_INSTRUCTIONS, the summary budget constants, anti-thrash)
         server/engine/recall.py — CJK detection, query splitting with AND / OR / NOT,
         the any-word retry, LIKE escaping and relative time bounds, adapted from
         hermes_state_search.py (_CJK_RANGES, _has_lone_cjk_run, _LIKE_TOKEN_RE,
         _compile_like_boolean_query, _or_relaxed_query), hermes_state_common.py
         (escape_like) and tools/session_search_tool.py (_RELATIVE_BOUND_RE, _parse_iso_bound)
         server/engine/when.py — schedule parsing (durations, clock times, day phrases, the
         "every" / "in" forms), the catch-up window and the DST fold handling for wall-clock
         schedules, adapted from cron/jobs.py (parse_duration, _parse_clock_time,
         _natural_every_to_cron, parse_schedule, _compute_grace_seconds, compute_next_run)
         server/engine/jobs.py — advance-before-run, the late / catch-up / missed one-shot
         policy and the scheduled-run hint (deliver by replying, [SILENT], no new jobs from a
         job run), adapted from cron/jobs.py (advance_next_run, get_due_jobs and helpers) and
         cron/scheduler_prompt.py (_CRON_HINT)
         server/engine/unattended.py — the silence markers, adapted from
         gateway/response_filters.py (LIVE_GATEWAY_SILENT_MARKERS, _strip_edge_silence_punctuation,
         is_intentional_silence_response, is_autonomous_silence_response); the inactivity
         watchdog and the delivery mirror, after cron/scheduler_liveness.py and gateway/mirror.py
         server/engine/sandbox.py (read at commit 219c6d2ac1cbecaea84c822f292c1e325dee06a0) —
         the container hardening flags and tmpfs mounts, removing a half-created container
         when docker create fails, and the proxy environment for the sandbox (both letter
         cases, NO_PROXY for loopback only), adapted from tools/environments/docker.py
         (_BASE_SECURITY_ARGS, _build_security_args, _docker_run) and
         tools/environments/docker_egress.py (_egress_proxy_args_for_docker)
         server/engine/host_exec.py (read at commit f6e272304e7224da88ca6e70e1c6ce4a67154f8e) —
         the dangerous-command patterns (the Unix ones: recursive deletes, world-writable
         permissions, disk formatting, download-and-execute, credential uploads, shell and
         system config writes, destructive git, …) and the command normalization before
         matching (ANSI escapes, NUL bytes, line continuations, quote and backslash tricks,
         $IFS, lowercasing that keeps flags), adapted from tools/approval_detection.py
         (HARDLINE_PATTERNS, DANGEROUS_PATTERNS, _normalize_command_for_detection,
         _lower_preserving_flags) and tools/ansi_strip.py (strip_ansi)

